      "artist": "Colin Smith",
      "description": "Provost Skene's House. This rubblestone building is one of the oldest left in Aberdeen. It was formerly houses in the old town, then became a lodging house. Today it houses one of the city's museums with period displays in each room. There is also a fine cafe on the ground floor which sells fine cakes and rowies!",
